# Line endings are decided here, not by each contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Everything in this repository is stored with LF, and with this file it is checked
# out as LF too. Without it, a clone on Windows gets CRLF in the working tree, and an
# editor that writes a file back that way turns a small change into a whole-file diff:
# every line differs, so the change cannot be reviewed line by line. It is a review
# problem rather than a build problem, and it is invisible until someone reads a
# diffstat and notices the numbers are far too large.
#
# mvnw is a POSIX shell script and must keep LF, which the rule below already gives it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the exception: the Windows command interpreter wants CRLF, and has
# been known to mis-handle multi-line constructs without it.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Declared explicitly so that a stray byte can never get one of these treated as text
# and mangled by end-of-line conversion.
*.ico   binary
*.jar   binary
*.png   binary
*.woff2 binary
